{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"5f9ddee7-9c0a-47cd-afcb-57b633e56d02","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[],"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/commands/check.ts","title":"Unused `manifest` variable in handleCheckRequest","rationale":"`handleCheckRequest` destructures `manifest` from `buildPipeline` return value but never reads it. `parseManifest` is called unnecessarily in request mode — only `graph.elements` is needed. TypeScript does not flag this (no `noUnusedLocals`).","line":96},{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/commands/check.ts","title":"check --request diagnostics hard-code line: 1","rationale":"`extractReferences` returns per-reference line numbers but the deduplication step discards the `Reference` objects, so all R0/R1/R2 diagnostics report `line: 1` regardless of actual source location. Storing the first `Reference` per targetId during deduplication would provide accurate line numbers.","line":133},{"severity":"low","file":"src/cli/commands/check-request.test.ts","title":"TC-029 (mixed citations: implemented + designed) not covered","rationale":"TC-029 is listed as 'should' priority in test-cases.md but has no corresponding test. The D7 per-element logic is correctly implemented in code but unprotected against regression. A test citing both an implemented and a designed element would protect this nuanced branch."},{"severity":"low","file":"spec/integration.md","title":"Diagnostic output format in integration.md not updated","rationale":"spec/integration.md §1 specifies `<LEVEL> <CODE> <id> <message>` (4 fields), but the implementation intentionally extends this to `<LEVEL> <CODE> <id> <message> (<file>:<line>)` per design.md D5. The external contract document has not been updated to reflect the extension."},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/design.md","title":"D7 first paragraph contradicts implemented per-element policy","rationale":"D7 opens with a statement that 'if any citation is designed/requested then implemented citations also pass', then immediately contradicts itself in the Rationale with the per-element judgment that was actually implemented. The first paragraph was superseded but not removed, leaving a misleading interpretation for future readers."}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0},"startedAt":"2026-07-02T05:08:04.264Z","endedAt":"2026-07-02T05:14:11.901Z"}
{"type":"lineage","step":"code-review","ts":"2026-07-02T05:14:11.901Z","outputs":[{"path":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/review-feedback-002.md","hash":null}],"inputs":[{"path":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/design.md","hash":"sha256:b7ab8cf14a43d212dc34888264fa7a0a3d6e7bbde8047297c5b8470aecc5db9e"},{"path":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/tasks.md","hash":"sha256:21dc464d741274bbe738b23cd7313acef89fca2febd15cd2b8f8ba89879a69bb"},{"path":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/test-cases.md","hash":"sha256:31b0de7c5f60ebee6f6d29464c574688f6aa1c2c71a1e80823e686cd0ef81c8d","required":false},{"path":".","hash":null}]}
