{"type":"step-attempt","step":"conformance","sessionId":"2ee70e47-89ee-45d1-b327-f59c2c04ae38","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/conformance-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/commands/check.ts","title":"Unused `manifest` variable in handleCheckRequest","rationale":"buildPipeline returns { graph, manifest } but manifest is never read in request mode. No runtime impact; TypeScript does not flag this without noUnusedLocals.","line":96,"fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/commands/check.ts","title":"R1/R2 diagnostics hard-code line: 1","rationale":"extractReferences returns per-reference line numbers, but the deduplication step discards Reference objects, losing source location precision. line: 1 is always a safe fallback but reduces diagnostic accuracy.","line":133,"fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/commands/check-request.test.ts","title":"TC-029 (mixed implemented+designed citations) not covered","rationale":"The should-priority test case for a request citing both an implemented and a designed element is absent. The D7 per-element logic is correctly implemented but unprotected against future refactoring.","fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"spec/integration.md","title":"Output format in spec/integration.md §1 does not include (<file>:<line>)","rationale":"Contract §1 specifies `<LEVEL> <CODE> <id> <message>` (4 fields). The implementation and spec.md correctly use the extended form with (<file>:<line>), but spec/integration.md has not been updated to reflect this.","line":15,"fixTarget":"spec-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"specrunner/changes/cli-check-wiring/design.md","title":"D7 first paragraph contradicts the per-element policy in the Rationale","rationale":"